===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|modal adverb}} [[without|Without]] [[doubt]], [[certainly]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Sure''' he's coming! Why wouldn't he?}}
#: {{ux|en|"Did you kill that bear yourself?" ―"I '''sure''' did!"}}
#: {{ux|en|It '''sure''' is cold out}}
#: {{ux|en|Isn’t there another way to do it? – '''Sure''' is, if you don’t mind going back home.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1802|author=w:Charles Lamb|title=John Woodvil
|passage=These high and gusty relishes of life, '''sure''',<br>Have no allayings of mortality in them.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[without fail|Without fail]], [[surely]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=iii|page=34|passage=Theſe are the wings ſhall make it flie as ſwift,<br>As dooth the lightening: or the breath of heauen,<br>And kill as '''ſure''' as it ſwiftly flies.}}

====Usage notes====
* Often proscribed in favor of {{m|en|surely}}. May be informal.

===Interjection===
{{en-intj}}

# {{lb|en|in response to a request for help or a favour}} [[yes|Yes]]; [[of course]].
#: {{ux|en|"Could you tell me where the washrooms are?" "'''Sure''', they're in the corner over there."}}
# {{lb|en|in response to other questions}} Yes; I [[guess]]; you [[could]] say that; {{non-gloss|a weak or noncommittal positive response}}.
#: {{ux|en|"Do you like cats?" "'''Sure'''."}}
#: {{ux|en|"Do you want me to put this in the garage?" "'''Sure''', go ahead."}}
# [[you're welcome|You're welcome]]; {{n-g|polite response to being thanked}}.
#: {{ux|en|"Thanks for helping me with that electrical fault." "'''Sure'''. Any time."}}
# {{lb|en|Ireland|for emphasis, sometimes repeated}} 
#: {{ux|en|"'''Sure''', I'm grand, '''sure'''."}}

====Usage notes====
* Occasionally used as an affirmative response even where "no" would be logical, as in: "Do you mind if I sit here?" "Sure."

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|noncommittal yes}} {{l|en|OK}} {{q|partial}}, {{l|en|yes}}
* {{sense|response to being thanked}} {{l|en|of course}}

